6 (All Saints, 2016)","section":"Multiple choice","marks":1,"topics":["Organic chemistry"],"subtopics":["Organic Chemistry"],"mixed":false,"text":"Which of the following statements are true about the compound represented by the formula below? I it decolourises bromine water. II it is soluble in water. III it undergoes addition reactions with hydrogen chloride to form two different isomers with the formula C4H9Cl. IV its systematic name is trans-2-butene.","html":"<div><p>Which of the following statements are true about the compound\nrepresented by the formula below?</p>\n<p><img src=\"assets/chemistry/practice-import-sixth/bf09d9cdbd3a823b49dbd783.webp\" alt=\"2016 Test 6 Organic Chemistry 1.docx — original diagram\" data-word-width-px=\"173.47\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"></p>\n<p>I it decolourises bromine water.</p>\n<p>II it is soluble in water.</p>\n<p>III it undergoes addition reactions with hydrogen chloride to form\ntwo different isomers with the formula C<sub>4</sub>H<sub>9</sub>Cl.</p>\n<p>IV its systematic name is trans-2-butene.</p>\n</div>","answerHtml":"<p>Supplied key: <strong>A</strong>.</p><div><p>I only.</p>\n</div>","options":["I only.","I and III only.","I, III and IV only.","I, II, III and IV."],"optionsHtml":["<div><p>I only.</p>\n</div>","<div><p>I and III only.</p>\n</div>","<div><p>I, III and IV only.</p>\n</div>","<div><p>I, II, III and IV.</p>\n</div>"],"correctAnswer":0,"markingMode":"automatic","solutionOrigin":"supplied","sourceFile":"2016 Test 6 Organic Chemistry 1.docx","sourcePath":"resources/ATAR/Chemistry/Assessments/12/All Saints/2016/2016 Test 6 Organic Chemistry 1.docx","sourceBlobSHA":"1ca8cfc67056fc1edb3c1efd0c14b844e9bc37a8","sourceSHA256":"ab414ae72a43f7484b13b6a9da1d6b4c599fe5db7cd6ae07b51841cdda1e63ee","sourceKeyFile":"2016 Test 6 Organic Chemistry 1 Answers.pdf","sourceKeyPath":"resources/ATAR/Chemistry/Assessments/12/All Saints/2016/2016 Test 6 Organic Chemistry 1 Answers.pdf","sourceKeyBlobSHA":"d7068a0743d7080